WEBVTT

00:00.150 --> 00:02.378
As far as this trip goes.

00:03.078 --> 00:09.816
Fifty-three million light-years: the black hole in M87, the first one ever photographed.

00:10.266 --> 00:16.085
The map goes further, to a quasar's black hole 10.8 billion light-years out.

00:16.535 --> 00:38.647
It shows 109 389 stars of the 1.8 billion Gaia has measured, 209 nebulae, clusters and galaxies (110 of them from OpenNGC's 13 372), and every confirmed planet around another star whose distance has been measured.

00:39.097 --> 00:42.970
The rest is out there; we have not drawn what we cannot place.
